Create a new app connection

Usage: vendo apps create [OPTIONS] --type <appType> --name <displayName>

Options:
      --profile <name>             Use a specific account profile
      --type <appType>             App type (e.g. google_ads, onesignal). See: vendo catalog list
      --debug                      Enable verbose request diagnostics
      --name <displayName>         Human-readable name for this connection
      --role <role>                Comma-separated capability: source, destination (derives default permissions) [default: source]
      --permissions <permissions>  Comma-separated granular permissions (e.g. performance_data,send_conversions). Overrides --role.
      --credentials-file <path>    Path to a JSON file with the credential payload
      --config-file <path>         Path to a JSON file with app-specific config
      --json                       Output raw JSON
      --output <field>             Print a single field (e.g. id)
  -h, --help                       Print help

Examples:
  $ vendo apps create --type onesignal --name "OneSignal Prod" --role destination --credentials-file onesignal.json
  $ vendo apps create --type bigquery --name "Analytics BQ" --role source --credentials-file bq-sa.json
